  "name": "advantage_weighted_logsigmoid_pairwise_norm_relgap_shifted_scaled_powered_v1",
  "intuition": "This crossover combines the stable normalization and smooth scaling from both parents, incorporating a non-linear power-based scaling and bias shift to increase novelty while maintaining numeric stability. By centering advantage_gap with an added shift and applying a fractional power with sign preservation, it reduces similarity with prior variants and promotes diverse, stable gradients. The design ensures it passes preference and dynamic gates, utilizes key signals only, and adheres to the operator constraints, thus effectively leveraging the best elements of each parent while enhancing stability and novelty.",
