  "intuition": "Fine-tuned the hyperparameters to improve stability and control over the loss landscape. Introduced a learned 'scale' hyperparam to dynamically adjust the tanh scaling, enabling better adaptation to different data distributions and preventing gradient explosion or vanishing. Maintained the normalization by advantage_gap norm plus epsilon to ensure numeric stability and symmetry. The clamping in the previous version was replaced by a learned scaling to balance between aggressive smoothing and preservation of distinctions. This hyperparameter-only tuning adjusts the scaling factor, which can be optimized via validation or grid search to enhance performance without disrupting the core loss structure. The family tags remain the same to preserve the intended paradigm, and the core logic stays consistent with the original, only adding the learned scale hyperparam.",
